# lore — Cursor Rules

This is a local-first AI chat history manager. See AGENTS.md for full guidelines.

## Key Rules

- All filesystem paths use `Path.home()` or `Path.expanduser()` — never hardcode `/home/...`
- New AI tool extractors go in `lore/extractors/` — inherit `BaseExtractor`, implement `tool`, `extract_sessions()`, `is_available()`
- Web routes in `lore/interfaces/web.py`; HTML templates in `web_templates.py` (Tailwind, no build step)
- Tests use `monkeypatch.setattr` — patch the **origin module** (`web_data`, `web_utils`, `web_jobs`), not the `web` namespace
- `RELOAD_JOBS` (in `web_jobs.py`) is in-memory; Gunicorn must run `--workers 1` or jobs will 404
- `load_index()` uses a file-stat LRU cache — call `clear_index_cache()` after any index write
- 100-char line limit, black + isort enforced

## Output Directory

All persistent data: `~/.lore/` (`OUTPUT_DIR` in `web_data.py`)
- `index.json` — flat session index
- `index.sqlite` — FTS search
- `projects/` — exported markdown sessions
